  "task": {
    "objective": "Cooperatively fill the nine mosaic cells with their hidden target colours, using exactly nine finite tiles, spatial access, public hints and transfers.",
    "natural_termination": "All nine board cells have irreversible tiles, whether correct or incorrect. Terminal shared reward is 2*(correct/9)-1. Otherwise truncate at 96 steps without a correctness payout.",
    "interaction": "A role's clue changes partner information; drawing and gifting change shared tile availability; placement consumes a unique tile and permanently closes that cell. Simultaneous resource/placement conflicts use public cyclic priority.",
    "observation_access": "The board, all hands, selected colours, urn supplies, ink, positions and disclosed hints are public. Role i privately sees only recipe row i. Undisclosed target colours do not enter public observations, legal masks or preterminal rewards. The known fixed map, including the mosaic floor, is fully walkable."
  },
